 and the lead differ.\n\nWorking through the fixed-point check, the other copy's action doesn't move with mine: with its input held at the prior, defecting dominates whatever it does, so the unique fixed point is defect-defect. Since there's only one fixed point, the policy fallback never kicks in, and I don't see a logical edge from my decision to the other copy's node because it evaluates the function on a different input. So the answer comes out as submitting the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out the decision under A-FDT as I've been reading it. In this Twin PD the two copies have different observations, so the other copy runs the same function on a different input. Intervening on my own decision leaves the other copy's action alone unless there is subjunctive dependence, and the other input differs, since the names and the lead differ.\n\nWorking through the fixed-point check, the other copy's action doesn't move with mine: with its input held at the prior, defecting dominates whatever it does, so the unique fixed point is defect-defect. Since there's only one fixed point, the policy fallback never kicks in, and I don't see a logical edge from my decision to the other copy's node because it evaluates the function on a different input. So the answer comes out as submitting the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9909,"completion_tokens":1037,"total_tokens":10946,"cost":0.060376,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.060376,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039636,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02074},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":597,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}